analysis:
I examined three changes.

(1) ProviderLoop+StartupPreload.swift head lines 302-308. After a startup preload run, finishStartupPreload now calls enqueueSelectedModelRecovery for summary.skippedInsufficientMemory, failedInsufficientMemory and notAttempted. It skips this when the task is cancelled, isShuttingDown is set or startupPreloadStopRequested is set. Self-test-retired ids (summary.retired/selfTestFailed) are not enqueued. The fail-closed retirement path (head 403-458, failedSelfTestHashes, isRefusedByRetirement) is unchanged.

The gate does not check servingDrain.refusing, unlike the updateAggregateCapacity call at head line 312. The ProviderLoop+SelectedModelRecovery implementation is not in this batch. Integration must verify that recovery:
- loads with allowEviction:false;
- re-checks advertisedModels, failedSelfTestHashes and retiringModels;
- honours servingDrain/add-on hold (TB-012, T-059, A-018), so models do not load beside running VMs;
- stops on shutdown, cancellation and logout;
- does not re-advertise a retired build (T-012/T-027 fail-closed intent).
This contract is unverified, so it is recorded here rather than as a finding.

(2) ProviderLoop+StartupShutdown.swift head lines 61 and 78-108. The unbounded shutdown unload loop is replaced by a per-slot bounded wait of 15s. A slot that does not finish unloading is abandoned and logged, and shutdown returns true; process exit releases the memory. Before this, unload ran only after the following had finished: inflight drain/cancel, coordinatorClient shutdown, stopAppAttestWorkerAndWait and drainNativeMiMoOwners. That ordering is unchanged. The unload Task is unstructured and may outlive the wait. ShutdownUnloadFlag is lock-guarded. Prompt plaintext (A-001) in a resident slot ends at process exit, so no new exposure was identified. Note that a true return now occurs with resident slots; callers treating true as 'fully unloaded' should be checked.

(3) ProviderLoop+Testing.swift head lines 514-525 adds internal test seams for the recovery load override. These are not externally reachable based on the visible code.

No concrete regression was established from the visible code.
